    "text_delta": "ritten Feedback\nTwo weeks without a reply is standard for academic hiring. Search committees typically cannot send written feedback until:\n1. The formal contract is signed and finalized with the selected candidate.\n2. The university's central HR or Dean’s office signs off on the search report and any written feedback.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n* **Do not raise the panel's gender makeup.** It will not provide leverage and will likely come across as adversarial without supporting a claim of sex discrimination.\n* **Follow up patiently:** Give it another week to ten days before sending a brief, polite follow-up email. Frame your request purely around professional development:\n  > *\"I understand the committee has a heavy schedule, but I would remain very grateful for any brief feedback or guidance that might help me strengthen future applications.\"*\n",
